  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WISA-YWP ZA-DK EXCHANGE PROGRAM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facilitate a knowledge and skills exchange of young water professionals from the North and South on key water and sanitation issues in the respective nations and global priorities to positively impact communities in South Africa and Denmark by: 
-	Gathering information during the WISA and IWA conferences that will partly inform YWP empowerment activities in both countries and in the development of short courses/training modules to upskill YWPs through IWA, WISA, EWSeta, Imvelisi and/or universities
-	Integrate unique individual and country expertise to come up with viable solutions to address skills shortage, high youth unemployment rates, lack of inclusivity in the water sector, inequalities in access to water and sanitation, etc
-	Sharing lessons learned and success stories from a young professionals&#x2019; perspective on navigating the national and global water challenges,
-	Identify and establish partnership with key stakeholders that will support the implementation of the project outcomes, 
-	Developing a position paper, and action plan that will contribute towards improving skills in the sector, empowering YWPs, building resilience, and ultimately solve poor technology adoption, lack of universal access to water and sanitation, by integrating unique country perspectives, and
-	Gathering information for the development of short courses/training modules to upskill YWPs</narrative>
  </description>
